Recently developed nanosheets and their composite membranes have enhanced stability and more possibilities for practical applications. The modification of 2D materials have improved the overall materials properties for membrane processes, solving the problems of previously developed 2D membranes. The modifications, such as chemical and physical crosslinking, functionalization, and inclusion in polymer nanocomposites, tightly bind the 2D nanosheets, which controls the space between nanosheets and its effects on molecular transport properties, and also increases dimensional stability. Various crosslinkers, such as linear and aromatic monomers with amide bonds, or polymers to physically entwine nanosheets with polymer chians, have been incorporated into 2D materials to build ultrathin nanocomposite membranes. After development of graphene materials, numerous graphene-like 2D materials have been investigated and widely reviewed in the precedent articles dealing with their physiochemical properties, fabrication approaches, and applications.[7] Synthetic methodologies in solution-based methods for constructing layered structures and
